      "content": "The key distinction often lies in intent and territorial alignment. A group \"just hanging out\" tends to be fluid in their positioning, engaging in casual interaction with their immediate environment. Conversely, a group displaying signs of a \"street crew\" often exhibits a rigid, cohesive formation, maintaining a barrier between themselves and the surrounding public. Look for shared, non-verbal communications—like specific nods or sudden, synchronized changes in posture—and an obvious possessive awareness toward a particular block or area, indicating territorial claim.",
